---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";

const REGISTERED_OFFICE = "Dorset House, 5 Church Street, Wimborne, Dorset, BH21 1JH";
const lastUpdated = "23 August 2026";
// Until the roofing company is confirmed the terms describe the arrangement
// without naming an entity that has not been verified at Companies House.
const hasContractor = Boolean(business.contractor.name);
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Roof Repairs Croydon"
  description="The terms on which this website is provided, who operates it, and who carries out the roofing work quoted through it."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="bg-ink text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        <a href="/" class="text-white hover:text-brand-light transition-colors">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
      </h1>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-light">Who you are dealing with, and on what basis</h2>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-base font-semibold text-steel-light">Last updated {lastUpdated}</h3>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-stone prose-a:text-brand-dark">
    <h2>Who operates this website</h2>
    <p>
      This website trades as {business.name} and is owned and operated by
      {" "}{business.siteOperator.name}, a company registered in England and Wales under number
      {" "}{business.siteOperator.companyNumber}, registered office {REGISTERED_OFFICE}.
    </p>

    <h2>Who carries out the roofing work</h2>
    {hasContractor ? (
      <p>
        {business.siteOperator.name} does not carry out roofing work. Surveys, quotations and the
        roofing itself are carried out by {business.contractor.name}, company number
        {" "}{business.contractor.companyNumber}. Any contract for roofing work is between you and
        that company, not between you and {business.siteOperator.name}.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        {business.siteOperator.name} does not carry out roofing work. Surveys, quotations and the
        roofing itself are carried out by a separate roofing company, whose identity and company
        number will be given to you in writing before any agreement is made. Any contract for
        roofing work is between you and that company, not between you and
        {" "}{business.siteOperator.name}.
      </p>
    )}
    <p>
      The role of {business.siteOperator.name} is to run this website and to pass your enquiry to
      that company. It does not survey roofs, does not issue quotations and is not a party to the
      work.
    </p>

    <h2>Enquiries and quotations</h2>
    <p>
      Submitting an enquiry does not create a contract and places you under no obligation. Surveys
      and written quotations are provided free of charge and without obligation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Quotations are fixed for the work described in them. The only circumstance in which a fixed
      price changes is where something not reasonably visible at the time of survey is found once
      work begins - for example rot in timber that was concealed by the roof covering. Where that
      is a realistic possibility on your roof, the quotation will say so before you accept it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guide prices published on this website, including on the roof repair cost page, are
      indicative bands to help you assess a quotation. They are not offers and they are not
      quotations.
    </p>

    <h2>Guarantees</h2>
    <p>
      Work booked through this website carries a {business.workmanshipGuaranteeYears} year
      workmanship guarantee, issued in writing by the company carrying out the work and provided to
      you on completion. Materials carry the relevant manufacturer's own warranty, which varies by
      product and is confirmed for your particular job.
    </p>
    <p>
      The workmanship guarantee covers the work carried out. It does not cover subsequent storm
      damage, damage caused by third parties, failure of parts of the roof not included in the
      work, or deterioration arising from a lack of ordinary maintenance such as clearing gutters.
    </p>

    <h2>Your cancellation rights</h2>
    <p>
      Where an agreement for work is made away from the contractor's business premises - which
      includes agreements made at your home - you normally have 14 days to cancel under the Consumer
      Contracts (Information, Cancellation and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013. If you ask for
      work to begin within that period and then cancel, you may be charged for what has already been
      done. Your cancellation rights are set out in full in the paperwork issued with the quotation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms affects your statutory rights under the Consumer Rights Act 2015,
      including the right to have services carried out with reasonable care and skill.
    </p>

    <h2>Content on this website</h2>
    <p>
      The guides, price bands and explanations on this site are general information about roofing in
      the Croydon area. They are not a substitute for somebody inspecting your roof, and no decision
      to spend or not spend money should rest on them alone. Planning and building control
      information is included in good faith and was correct when written, but rules change and vary
      by authority. Always confirm your own position with the relevant council before relying on it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Text, images and layout on this site belong to {business.siteOperator.name} or are used under
      licence, and may not be reproduced without permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for
      fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited. Subject to that,
      {" "}{business.siteOperator.name}'s liability in connection with this website is limited to
      the operation of the website itself, and liability in respect of roofing work rests with the
      company that carried it out.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales
      have jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {business.siteOperator.name}, {REGISTERED_OFFICE}.<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a><br />
      Telephone: <a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phone}</a>
    </p>
    <p>See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
